# `const N = {}` and then `N.a = 1; ..`: the literal writes NOTHING; its names come from the stores behind it. A literal ALL of whose names are functions has a layout of its own file; of a literal
# without a name "all" is true and says nothing: so N had a layout of its own file (L0) beside the layout of the names a, b, c, d (L1), `{ ...N, a: i }` no longer copied field by field
# (TryCopyFields) and took CopyDataProperties at every turn: 5,115 > 24,430 instructions a call of f. f1 = f . L0 = the one layout of the names a, b, c, d.
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK: = TryCopyFields {{*}}layout=L0
# -- source: an-object-filled-behind-an-empty-literal-has-the-layout-of-its-names.cjs
